<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    angr test_switch_case_shared_case_nodes_b2sum_digest: kuna fails to recover the
    getopt_long option-dispatch switch in coreutils b2sum's main and renders the
    BRANCHIND as an indirect *call* (goto spaghetti), where angr recovers a real
    11-case switch (incl. the 132->98 "shared case node" fallthrough).
    Opportunity: docs/features/switch-case-shared-case-node-0e34ba/.

    The bytes below are the real GCC-compiled `main` of
    b2sum-digest_shared_switch_nodes.o, linked to a fixed base (main @ 0x401000,
    the relative-offset jump table @ 0x403d60) so the testcase is self-contained
    (the external getopt_long/dcgettext/... calls remain unresolved calls, which is
    irrelevant to jump-table recovery; only `main` + the .rodata table are needed,
    and all 35 table targets land inside `main`).

    The construct is a textbook GCC PIC relative-offset jump table whose base
    register (`lea .rodata, %rbp` @ 0x401071) is established ONCE before the getopt
    `while` loop while the BRANCHIND (`movslq (%rbp,%rax,4); add %rbp; notrack jmp`
    @ 0x4010fd..0x401105) is INSIDE it:

        sub  $0x62,%eax            ; normalize index (idx = getopt result - 98)
        cmp  $0x22,%eax ; ja       ; the bound: idx <=u 0x22  (35 entries)
        movslq 0x0(%rbp,%rax,4),%rax  ; load signed int32 table offset
        add  %rbp,%rax             ; target = base + offset
        notrack jmp *%rax          ; BRANCHIND

    Root cause (S2 "switch-model"): the table base reaches the jump through a
    loop-header MULTIEQUAL and feeds BOTH the load address (base + idx*4) and the
    final add (base + offset), so JumpBasic::findDeterminingVarnodes melds the two
    paths down to the single final INT_ADD.  The normalized index (the value the
    out-of-band `cmp $0x22; ja` guard bounds) never enters the path-meld, so
    findSmallestNormal leaves it unbounded, recover_model builds no model, and
    truncateIndirectJump downgrades the BRANCHIND to a CALLIND ("Treating indirect
    jump as call").

    Fix surface = a default-off ArchOption (switchsharedcase): when the normal
    model and the modulo/CBRANCH-guard extensions all fail, walk the index path
    from the BRANCHIND down through the realigning ops and the one table LOAD to
    the guarded load index, collect the loop-invariant `lea .rodata` base and seed
    it into the emulation, rebuild the meld as a clean single path to that index,
    and re-run findNormalized so the table sizes at 35 and the switch structures.

    Pass 1 (default, option off): assertion #1 proves the bug reproduces; the
    dispatch downgrades to an indirect call ("// jump-as-call").
    Assertion #2 (switch count == 1) proves NO switch is recovered on the off pass
    (the single match comes from the option-on pass only).
    Pass 2 (option switchsharedcase on): assertion #2 proves the table is bounded
    and the dispatch is recovered as a single `switch(idx - 0x62){...}` (no more
    "Too many branches" / computed call).
-->
